#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193729} :activity/id #uuid "bda8a4b6-826f-51a7-8a70-7a94506cabca" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048312 :topic/id #uuid "93c53f5b-1566-5fb9-ab22-72c79a0d93e3" :topic/math-academy-id 4034} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193729 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193914 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the following inequality: \n\n$$\n7x -2 < 5x - 18\n$$\n\nAs usual, we solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle. We start by subtracting $5x$ from both sides: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-2 & <5x-18 \\\\ 7x-2-5x & <5x-18-5x \\\\ 2x-2 & <-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $2$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & <-18 \\\\ 2x-2+2 & <-18+2 \\\\ 2x & <-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & <-16 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & <\\frac{-16}{2} \\\\ x & <-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x < -8.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e1c6e185-0d13-5ea0-86f9-e61f64898f5f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8106 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "cc58d969-cf99-5cc9-b7d4-80118ddd2859" :step/math-academy-id 52148 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193730}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193730 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192821 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192543 :question/id #uuid "9f887f78-3ba8-540d-af89-1c3166ee6c38" :question/math-academy-id "e-12970"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dd6988a-86b8-5b56-bf3e-fc0df20e099b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048213} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048483}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193333} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193371} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507437} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507516}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities With Variables on Both Sides"} :step/id #uuid "591346ba-99a7-5721-93c2-821ddfaef9a8" :step/math-academy-id 52170 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193731}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193731 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193915 :tutorial/content "Now, let's solve an inequality that contains a rational expression:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2y-1}{3} \\lt 5\n$$\n\nFirst, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y-1}{3} & <5 \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2y-1}{3}) & <3\\cdot 5 \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2y-1}{\\cancel{3}}) & <15 \\\\ 2y-1 & <15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-1 & <15 \\\\ 2y-1+1 & <15+1 \\\\ 2y & <16 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & <\\frac{16}{2} \\\\ y & <8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y <  8.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "31078899-8e97-5c79-a990-df51f4a9f773" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8107 :tutorial/title "Clearing Rational Expression in Linear Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "ebbe6b5a-54bb-59dd-88b0-1e010c9ed541" :step/math-academy-id 52173 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193732}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193732 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192822 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192544 :question/id #uuid "232b1ad9-6651-582b-b942-b36c7896806e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12971"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "215dc4e3-bf30-538d-bc8c-d67d6a60e12b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048760}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192941} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192942} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507426} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507456} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507503}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing a Rational Expression"} :step/id #uuid "ac05f5cd-fcfd-545f-8716-67c2baa838d3" :step/math-academy-id 52179 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193733}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193733 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192823 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192545 :question/id #uuid "bab434ec-d18a-5d77-9bf1-8e16e9af2556" :question/math-academy-id "e-12974"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9374b546-aa83-53f6-b38d-fc750350e659" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050908}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193306} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193309} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507475} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507491}] :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities With Rational Expression and Variables on Both Sides"} :step/id #uuid "b9448a32-13ac-535e-a4d8-7cd491b8a4d9" :step/math-academy-id 52183 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193734}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193734 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193916 :tutorial/content "Finally, let's consider an inequality that contains rational expressions on both sides:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x+1}{4} \\leq \\dfrac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nThe rational expressions on both sides of this inequality have positive denominators $4$ and $2.$ The least common multiple of $4$ and $2$ is ${\\color{red}{4}}.$\nThus, we can clear the rational expressions by multiplying both sides of the inequality ${\\color{red}{4}}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{4} & \\le \\frac{x}{2} \\\\ 4\\cdot (\\frac{x+1}{4}) & \\le 4\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}) \\\\ x+1 & \\le 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. \n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & \\le 2x \\\\ x+1-2x & \\le 2x-2x \\\\ 1-x & \\le 0 \\\\ 1-x-1 & \\le 0-1 \\\\ -x & \\le -1 \\\\ \\frac{-x}{(-1)} & \\,\\,\\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-1}{(-1)} \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\geq 1.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "5ec24500-fe0f-5068-b9fa-f19ce733798a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8110 :tutorial/title "Clearing Two Rational Expressions in Linear Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "7036141e-7fee-5677-9ad3-d8da3867d41f" :step/math-academy-id 52187 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193735}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193735 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192824 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192546 :question/id #uuid "8740f864-62be-5391-bf06-ac4f4e1c1a2c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12975"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a00ac76c-0ebd-53cb-b689-98bda731064a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049846}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193126} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193127} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507419} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507467} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507506}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inequalities by Clearing Two Rational Expressions"} :step/id #uuid "d4683a11-1cf6-5a10-a65e-969247f24091" :step/math-academy-id 52192}] :activity/title "Further Solving Linear Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192910}]}
